  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Start Ready Senegal Risk Pool 4 2025</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The department of Bambey in the Diourbel region, more precisely in its northeastern part, continues to persist in precariousness, vulnerability to food insecurity and malnutrition. No assistance included in the National Response Plan (NRP) from the government or its partners has been recorded, thus leaving this department to the vagaries of malnutrition and the food crisis. Since then, Bambey has struggled with this food and nutrition insecurity which must be acted on in order to avoid the pangs of malnutrition. The lack of rain, the unsuitable seed seed, the low rainfall mixed with the presence of insect pests have ended up endangering the endangered target population, giving a glimpse of a dark future for its communities. General objective: To contribute to the reduction of food and nutrition insecurity in the department of Bambey. SO1: Increase the livelihoods of vulnerable households during the crisis period through a cash transfer mechanism. 0S2: Strengthen prevention of malnutrition in targeted households, especially among children under 5 years of age and pregnant and lactating women. SO3: Promote climate -resilient agricultural practices in this agro -ecological zone to the peasant communities of the intervention area.&quot;</narrative>
  </description>
